  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 29,
    "summary": "Job recalls his former prosperity and greatness—He was blessed because of his righteousness, his charity, and his good deeds.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Moreover Job continued his parable, and said,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 29:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Oh that I were as in months past, as in the days when God preserved me;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 20
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 39
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 29:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "When his candle shined upon my head, and when by his light I walked through darkness;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "OR lamp."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 45
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 75
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 29:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "As I was in the days of my youth, when the secret of God was upon my tabernacle;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "OR friendship, confidence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 60
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 29:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "When the Almighty was yet with me, when my children were about me;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 21
          },
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 39
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 56
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 29:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "When I washed my steps with butter, and the rock poured me out rivers of oil;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 29:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "When I went out to the gate through the city, when I prepared my seat in the street!",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 29:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "The young men saw me, and hid themselves: and the aged arose, and stood up.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 29:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "The princes refrained talking, and laid their hand on their mouth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 29:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "The nobles held their peace, and their tongue cleaved to the roof of their mouth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 29:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "When the ear heard me, then it blessed me; and when the eye saw me, it gave witness to me:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 22
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 29:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Because I delivered the poor that cried, and the fatherless, and him that had none to help him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "Mosiah 4:26; D&C 42:31 (30–31); 104:18."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 77
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 29:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "The blessing of him that was ready to perish came upon me: and I caused the widow’s heart to sing for joy.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 29:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "I put on righteousness, and it clothed me: my judgment was as a robe and a diadem.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "TG Righteousness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 58
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Righteousness.",
            "prettyString": "TG Righteousness",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
